# Build context exclusions.
#
# Both Dockerfiles do `COPY . /app`, so anything reachable here is baked into the
# image and survives in a layer even if a later step deletes it. The previous
# list excluded `.env` exactly, which does not cover `.env.production`,
# `.env.local`, a stray key, or a database dump - and this repo root is where
# scratch files accumulate (CONTRIBUTING warns against `git add -A` for the same
# reason). Untracked files are the risk: they are invisible to gitleaks, which
# scans git history, but fully visible to the Docker build.
#
# Verified before tightening: of everything tracked, only .env.example matches
# the new patterns, and it is re-included below.

# --- secrets and credentials ---------------------------------------------
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.token
*token.txt
*.secret
secrets.json
.ssh/
.aws/
.gnupg/
# Deliberately NOT using catch-alls like *secret* or *credential*: they match
# real source modules (credential_vault.py, credential_encryption.py,
# named_credential.xml.j2) and would silently drop them from the image, turning a
# hardening change into an ImportError at boot.

# --- data dumps -----------------------------------------------------------
*.sql
*.dump
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.bak

# --- vcs, caches, build junk ---------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
*.pyc
__pycache__
venv/
.venv/
node_modules/
*.tar.gz
*.zip
*.7z
*.log
*.jsonl
*.bundle

# --- test / analysis artefacts -------------------------------------------
tests/
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.coverage*
.pytest_cache/
.scannerwork/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
sa_test_screenshots/
audit/

# --- not needed at runtime ------------------------------------------------
docs/
agents/
scripts/guardrails/
# migrations/versions/ is NOT excluded: schema-upgrade (ADR 0002) applies these
# revisions on deploy from inside the built image, so the image must ship them.
.claude/
.serena/
.cursor/
.github/
*.bat
*.ps1
-w
deploy/.dockerignore
